WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.118
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online IELTS preparation.

2
00:00:05.418 --> 00:00:08.735
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.035 --> 00:00:17.922
Unit eighteen: Speaking Part 1: Familiar Topics. Today you will answer short personal questions fluently with reasons and examples.

4
00:00:18.222 --> 00:00:20.746
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:25.235
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:26.083 --> 00:00:27.026
Hometown.

7
00:00:28.017 --> 00:00:30.260
Hometown means the place where you grew up.

8
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:32.513
My hometown is Siem Reap.

9
00:00:33.117 --> 00:00:35.734
Your turn. Say: Hometown.

10
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:39.543
Hometown.

11
00:00:40.283 --> 00:00:41.296
Routine.

12
00:00:42.283 --> 00:00:44.991
Routine means your usual daily activities.

13
00:00:45.583 --> 00:00:47.374
My routine starts at six.

14
00:00:47.983 --> 00:00:50.984
Your turn. Say: Routine.

15
00:00:53.833 --> 00:00:54.869
Routine.

16
00:00:55.617 --> 00:00:56.420
Hobby.

17
00:00:57.417 --> 00:01:00.612
Hobby means an activity you enjoy in your free time.

18
00:01:01.217 --> 00:01:02.856
My hobby is cooking.

19
00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:06.288
Your turn. Say: Hobby.

20
00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:09.833
Hobby.

21
00:01:10.583 --> 00:01:11.515
Extend.

22
00:01:12.517 --> 00:01:14.957
Extend means to make an answer longer.

23
00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:17.491
Extend your answer with a reason.

24
00:01:18.083 --> 00:01:20.306
Your turn. Say: Extend.

25
00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:24.237
Extend.

26
00:01:24.983 --> 00:01:25.915
Fluency.

27
00:01:26.917 --> 00:01:30.228
Fluency means speaking smoothly without long pauses.

28
00:01:30.817 --> 00:01:32.921
Fluency is a marking criterion.

29
00:01:33.517 --> 00:01:36.401
Your turn. Say: Fluency.

30
00:01:39.267 --> 00:01:40.221
Fluency.

31
00:01:40.983 --> 00:01:41.799
Filler.

32
00:01:42.783 --> 00:01:45.712
Filler means a word like well that gives thinking time.

33
00:01:46.317 --> 00:01:47.933
Use fillers naturally.

34
00:01:48.517 --> 00:01:51.169
Your turn. Say: Filler.

35
00:01:54.033 --> 00:01:54.802
Filler.

36
00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:56.737
Pronunciation.

37
00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.156
Pronunciation means the way you say words.

38
00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:03.179
Clear pronunciation helps the examiner.

39
00:02:03.783 --> 00:02:06.691
Your turn. Say: Pronunciation.

40
00:02:09.533 --> 00:02:10.941
Pronunciation.

41
00:02:11.683 --> 00:02:12.615
Opinion.

42
00:02:13.617 --> 00:02:15.825
Opinion means what you think about something.

43
00:02:16.417 --> 00:02:18.068
Give a reason for your opinion.

44
00:02:18.683 --> 00:02:21.289
Your turn. Say: Opinion.

45
00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:24.960
Opinion.

46
00:02:25.767 --> 00:02:29.359
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:30.217 --> 00:02:32.425
Visal, what is Speaking Part 1?

48
00:02:33.517 --> 00:02:44.981
It is a four- to five-minute conversation about familiar topics such as your home, work, studies and hobbies. The examiner asks about nine or ten short questions.

49
00:02:46.083 --> 00:02:47.886
How long should my answers be?

50
00:02:48.983 --> 00:03:00.796
Aim for two or three sentences. Answer the question, give a reason, and add a short example, for instance: I like cooking because it relaxes me, and I often cook for my family.

51
00:03:01.883 --> 00:03:03.279
What should I avoid?

52
00:03:04.383 --> 00:03:19.354
Avoid one-word answers and memorised speeches. Examiners listen for natural fluency, so pause briefly and use fillers like well or let me think, but do not overuse them.

53
00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.209
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:27.325
Grammar focus: Strategy: answer plus reason plus example.

55
00:03:27.625 --> 00:03:28.812
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:29.517 --> 00:03:31.795
I like cooking because it relaxes me.

57
00:03:32.683 --> 00:03:35.159
I often cook for my family on weekends.

58
00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:43.675
Answer in two or three sentences: answer, reason, example. Speak naturally and avoid one-word answers and memorised speeches.

59
00:03:44.417 --> 00:03:47.963
Be careful! Don't say: I answer only 'Yes' or 'No'.

60
00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:52.422
Say: I answer, give a reason and an example.

61
00:03:52.722 --> 00:03:54.176
Extend your answers.

62
00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:57.712
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:00.337
A Part 1 Conversation.

64
00:04:00.637 --> 00:04:03.322
The examiner asks Chenda about her hometown.

65
00:04:04.333 --> 00:04:07.587
She says she comes from Battambang, a calm and friendly city.

66
00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:12.028
She explains that the river and old buildings make it special.

67
00:04:13.033 --> 00:04:16.043
She gives an example of a weekend market she enjoys.

68
00:04:17.033 --> 00:04:19.312
The examiner moves to the next question.

69
00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:24.355
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:25.217 --> 00:04:26.996
Part 1 lasts about blank.

71
00:04:27.296 --> 00:04:31.646
A, four to five minutes. B, twenty minutes. C, one minute.

72
00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:38.082
The answer is A: four to five minutes.

73
00:04:39.217 --> 00:04:42.099
A good answer has an answer, a blank and an example.

74
00:04:42.399 --> 00:04:45.170
A, graph. B, reason. C, map.

75
00:04:48.733 --> 00:04:51.046
The answer is B: reason.

76
00:04:52.183 --> 00:04:53.533
Which should you avoid?

77
00:04:53.833 --> 00:04:58.136
A, reasons. B, examples. C, one-word answers.

78
00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:04.141
The answer is C: one-word answers.

79
00:05:05.283 --> 00:05:06.563
Where is Chenda from?

80
00:05:06.863 --> 00:05:10.725
A, Battambang. B, Phnom Penh. C, Siem Reap.

81
00:05:14.267 --> 00:05:16.255
The answer is A: Battambang.

82
00:05:17.417 --> 00:05:19.091
Fillers should be used blank.

83
00:05:19.391 --> 00:05:23.613
A, never. B, sparingly. C, in every sentence.

84
00:05:27.167 --> 00:05:29.375
The answer is B: sparingly.

85
00:05:30.567 --> 00:05:33.683
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:36.782
Tell me about your hometown, with a reason.

87
00:05:45.583 --> 00:05:47.002
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:47.302 --> 00:05:57.887
I come from a small city by the river. I like it because it is calm and friendly. For example, on weekends I often visit the market with my family and eat local food.

89
00:05:58.187 --> 00:06:00.001
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:00.917 --> 00:06:06.913
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: answer plus reason plus example.

91
00:06:07.213 --> 00:06:11.421
Today's value is confidence. Speak up and be proud of who you are.

92
00:06:11.721 --> 00:06:14.640
See you in Unit nineteen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:17.755
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

